      "id": "C1",
      "text": "c_direct and c_batched are counted with the schoolbook F_{p^2} multiplication unit on one frozen j-list, and Delta is recomputed at the exact prime, not read from the rounded row.",
      "class": "exact_computation",
      "decided_by": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "text": "c >= 2^Delta, so the listing correction lifts the NIST-I time lower bound to at least the Delfs-Galbraith line under the Section 4.1 model.",
